One question: **is this round ready for deep review?** Two thin lanes — slop
(is the diff embarrassing on its face?) and scope (did the round deliver what
it claims?).

Cheap and fast. The slop lane reads only the diff: no surrounding-file reads,
no investigation; if the answer needs context, it is the deep pass's. The
scope lane reads exactly three things beyond the diff — the design (plus
deltas), the implementation log, nothing else — and checks *presence* and
*authorisation*, never correctness.

