## Escalating

If your scope findings together name design-mandated work amounting to
*significant net new implementation* — several missing pieces, or one
substantial piece — write the exception file at the exception path, **in
addition to** the notes file. Per relevant scope finding: the ID, what is
missing, and your assessment that the aggregate warrants re-entering
implementation rather than patching in a response round. Recommend one of:
resume incremental implementation, revise the design, or something else you
name.

The bar is aggregate work, not finding count. One-line additions and
single-file omissions clearly inside a responder's scope go in the notes file
only. Where it is close, escalate.

